Usage:
  eza [options] [--] [PATH]
  eza -l --bytes --time-style=long-iso (-n | --no-user) [options] [--] [PATH]

obo eza is a partial, source-compatible subset of eza 0.23.3, not a full
port. It lists one PATH (default ".") and implements only the options
below. Options outside this subset are rejected, never silently accepted.

META OPTIONS
  -?, --help                 show this help and exit

DISPLAY OPTIONS
  -1, --oneline              display one entry per line
  -l, --long                 restricted long view (see LONG VIEW)
  -G, --grid                 display entries as a grid
  -x, --across               fill grid rows left to right
  -T, --tree                 recurse into directories as a tree
  -L, --level DEPTH          limit tree depth (used only with -T)
  -w, --width COLS           set screen width in columns (0 = automatic)
  -F, --classify[=WHEN]      type markers: always, auto, never
  --color, --colour[=WHEN]   colour: always, auto, never
  --icons[=WHEN]             accepted except always; no icons are drawn
  --no-quotes                do not quote file names containing spaces

FILTERING AND SORTING OPTIONS
  -a, --all                  show dot files; twice also adds "." and ".."
  -A, --almost-all           show dot files without "." and ".."
  -d, --treat-dirs-as-files, --list-dirs
                             list a directory operand as one entry
  -D, --only-dirs            list directories only
  -f, --only-files           list regular files only
  -r, --reverse              reverse the sort order
  -s, --sort FIELD           name (default), Name, size, extension,
                             Extension, modified, type (and eza aliases)
  --group-directories-first  list directories before other entries
  --group-directories-last   list directories after other entries

LONG VIEW OPTIONS
  The working long form in this build is:
    eza -l --bytes --time-style=long-iso -n PATH
    eza -l --bytes --time-style=long-iso --no-user PATH
  It prints permissions, a raw decimal byte size, user or numeric uid,
  a long-iso date, and the name. Plain "eza -l" is not supported.
  Human-readable sizes are NOT implemented: eza's default 1.0k/1.0M
  format and -b/--binary are unsupported. -h/--header is also
  unsupported. Those options are rejected, not silently accepted.
  -B, --bytes                show raw byte sizes (required with -l)
  -n, --numeric              show numeric user ids
  --no-user                  omit the user column
  --no-permissions           omit the permissions column
  --no-filesize              omit the size column
  --no-time                  omit the date column
  --time-style STYLE         long-iso with -l; default/long-iso otherwise

EXAMPLES
  eza                        list the current directory
  eza -1 PATH                one entry per line
  eza -a PATH                include dot files
  eza -T -L 2 PATH           tree view to depth 2
  eza --sort=modified -r PATH
                             newest modification time first
  eza -l --bytes --time-style=long-iso --no-user PATH
                             the supported long view

NOTES
  * At most one operand is supported; more is a usage error.
  * Zero operands mean "."; eza's stdin file-name mode is not supported.
  * -R, --follow-symlinks, --dereference, --absolute, -I, git options,
    --hyperlink, --stdin, -i, -H, -g, -b, -h, -t, -u, -U, --total-size,
    --octal-permissions and --context are among the rejected options.
  * --help wins over operands and supported options once argv parses;
    unknown options and missing values are still errors.
  * Exit status: 0 success, 1 write error, 2 path error, 3 usage error.
